# copyxform

- Label: Copy and Transform
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 80 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/copyxform.html
- Summary (EN): Copy and Transform (copyxform) makes copies of an input stamp and applies successive transformations to each copy. The original stamp stays untouched.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Copy and Transform copie un tampon et applique à chaque copie des transformations cumulées, sans modifier l'original.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets output image size and metadata", "shape: layer containing the stamp to copy and transform", "pointmask (optional): limits which copies are stamped, based on location"]

- Key parameters: ["Total Number: total copies including the original", "Order: sequence in which Translate, Rotate and Scale are applied", "Translate / Rotate / Scale: move, rotate (degrees, Z axis) and stretch or compress; Uniform Scale multiplies X and Y", "Center Pivot on Shape, Pivot Translate, Pivot Rotate", "Blend Method: Over, Under, Add, Subtract, Multiply, Maximum, Minimum", "Filter: sampling method", "Wrap Mode / Tile Size: copies outside the main tile wrap back in, for seamless repeats", "Stamp Color, Change per Copy, Color Ramp", "Uniform Alpha, Alpha Ramp", "Background Color / Background Alpha"]

- Caveats: ["Transformations are cumulative, each copy builds on the previous one", "Over and Under presort copies by creation order, which can be expensive", "Color Ramp disables Change per Copy; Alpha Ramp disables its per-copy counterpart", "With Wrap Mode set to Auto, wrapping depends on the Border type of size_ref"]

